::Q1::What is zero shot prompting? 
{
=Asking the model to perform a task without providing worked examples
~Providing several worked examples before the task
~Training a model from scratch
~Fine tuning a model for the task
}

::Q2::What is few shot or multi shot prompting? 
{
=Including one or more worked examples in the prompt
~Using no examples at all
~Changing the model's training weights automatically
~Removing the task instruction
}

::Q3::What is one advantage of multi shot prompting? 
{
~It guarantees factual accuracy
=Examples can demonstrate the expected pattern and improve consistency
~It eliminates the need for task instructions
~It always makes prompts shorter
}

::Q4::What is a good starting strategy for many prompting tasks? 
{
~Fine tune before writing a prompt
~Always begin with dozens of examples
=Start with zero shot prompting and add examples if more consistency is needed
~Never use examples under any circumstance
}

::Q5::Why should prompt examples be chosen carefully? 
{
=Poor or inconsistent examples can teach the model an unclear pattern
~Examples are never considered by the model
~Examples eliminate all ambiguity regardless of their content
~Examples automatically become permanent model weights
}